;UFNTER:  ENTER OPCODE (D/E/F/P/S/Q... ):$
*T ==> The "gsmoo2" utility is used for smoothing of f(x,y) 2d Ufiles.
;UFNTER:  ENTER OPCODE (D/E/F/P/S/Q... ):$
H ACS ECS Q
;UFNTER:  ENTER OPCODE (D/E/F/P/S/Q... ):$
P S Q
;GSMOO2:  ENTER 5 DIGIT SHOT #, "Q" TO QUIT, "D" TO CHANGE NAMES$
37065
;GSMOO2:  ENTER SMOOTHING OPTION (1/2/I/W/G ... ):$
G 1 P Q Q
;GSMOO2:  ENTER SMOOTHING OPTION (1/2/I/W/G ... ):$
*T The program supports units transformation on the data
U
;UCHUNS:  ENTER NEW UNITS (10 CHAR LABEL) OR "0" NOT TO CHANGE:$
KEV
;UCHUNS:  ENTER CONVERSION FACTOR A: (NEW UNITS PER OLD UNIT)$
0.001
;UCHUNS:  ENTER OFFSET B (QUANTITY TO ADD OR FACTOR INTO DATA):$
0.000
;UCHUNS:  ENTER NEW UNITS (10 CHAR LABEL) OR "0" NOT TO CHANGE:$
0
;UCHUNS:  ENTER NEW UNITS (10 CHAR LABEL) OR "0" NOT TO CHANGE:$
0
;GSMOO2:  ENTER SMOOTHING OPTION (1/2/I/W/G ... ):$
G 1 P Q Q
;GSMOO2:  ENTER SMOOTHING OPTION (1/2/I/W/G ... ):$
*T Smoothing can be along either dimension (frequency smooth follows)...
2
; SUB:USMOO2 >> ENTER OPTION #:$
3
; USMOO2:  INTERCHANGE INDEPENDANT VARIABLE? (Y/N):$
N
; SUB:PCIDEF >> ENTER OPTION #:$
1
; SUB:PCIDEF > ENTER NEW X VALUE:$
210
; SUB:PCIDEF > ENTER NEW Y VALUE:$
10
; SUB:PCIDEF >> ENTER OPTION #:$
5
; SUB:USMOO2 >> ENTER OPTION #:$
10
; USMOO2: ENTER "Y" TO PLOT DELTA (FINAL):$
N
; SUB:USMOO2 >> ENTER OPTION #:$
11
;GSMOO2:  ENTER SMOOTHING OPTION (1/2/I/W/G ... ):$
G 1 P Q Q
;GSMOO2:  ENTER SMOOTHING OPTION (1/2/I/W/G ... ):$
*T Time smooth follows (this will require a few seconds of cpu time)...
1
; SUB:USMOO2 >> ENTER OPTION #:$
3
; USMOO2:  INTERCHANGE INDEPENDANT VARIABLE? (Y/N):$
N
; SUB:PCIDEF >> ENTER OPTION #:$
1
; SUB:PCIDEF > ENTER NEW X VALUE:$
0
; SUB:PCIDEF > ENTER NEW Y VALUE:$
.08
; SUB:PCIDEF >> ENTER OPTION #:$
5
; SUB:USMOO2 >> ENTER OPTION #:$
10
; USMOO2: ENTER "Y" TO PLOT DELTA (FINAL):$
N
; SUB:USMOO2 >> ENTER OPTION #:$
11
;GSMOO2:  ENTER SMOOTHING OPTION (1/2/I/W/G ... ):$
G 1 P Q Q
;GSMOO2:  ENTER SMOOTHING OPTION (1/2/I/W/G ... ):$
*T GSMOO2 will also do an axes swap f(x,y) -> f(y,x)
*T allowing user to change axis of contiguous storage of the data
I
;GSMOO2:  ENTER SMOOTHING OPTION (1/2/I/W/G ... ):$
G 1 P Q Q
;GSMOO2:  ENTER SMOOTHING OPTION (1/2/I/W/G ... ):$
Q
